# The build writes LF. Without this, Git's autocrlf on Windows rewrites every
# generated file to CRLF on checkout, so the next `node build.js` reports the
# whole of extension/ and dist/ as modified even when nothing changed. Pinning
# them to LF keeps build output diffable: a dirty file then means a real change.
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
